but I did not feel like having all my stuff cursed before meeting Vecna.

I started zapping him from a distance with mostly magic missile and 
stream of acid spells.  (He is definitely cold resistant and I presume 
also fire resistant, so bolt of cold and fireball are of little use.) 
What I realized then is that Vecna is *very slow* at waking up from his 
meditation.  I think I got five or six spells at him, taking him down 
from 313 Hp (seen by a wand of probing) to 30ish.  Then I went to him 
and finished him off with two hits from the +7 Excalibur.  I had quaffed 
a potion of invulnerability before, just to make sure.  It also 
protected me from the blast when picking up the Key of Chaos.

 From my two encounters with Vecna it appears to me that he did not wake 
up, before I went to melee distance.  If this is a rule, then you can 
*always* kill him safely by being able to either cast aforesaid spells 
often enough or having a bunch of +7 daggers in addition.  But it may 
simply be that he will always wake up with a certain probability. 
Otherwise things would be too easy.
